# Ocean TD rules

## Read order
1. `docs/PROJECT_OVERVIEW.md`
2. `docs/SYSTEMS_INDEX.md` for the system you touch
3. Only then open the 2–4 listed scripts
Do not broad-scan the repo unless the index is missing — then fix the index.

## Source of truth
- Server owns place, pay, persist, plot ownership, scores.
- Client mirrors (previews, camera, UI). No parallel authority.
- Layout is plot-local; grid math constants must match on server and client.
- Plots: `MasterTerrainBox` + plugin `PreviewBox_1..5` (no Arena.Center). Décor: author `MasterPlotDecor`; boot clones → `StaticPlot_N`. See `docs/STUDIO_CONTRACT.md`.

## Persistence (sacred)
- Never save while `layoutLoaded` is false.
- Never overwrite a non-empty DataStore layout with an empty snapshot unless intentional clear.
- DataStores: join / leave / autosave only — not per frame.
- One persist shape: extend `PersistenceService` + `PlotTypes`; see `docs/PERSISTENCE_CONTRACT.md`.

## UI
- Default generated text font: `Enum.Font.FredokaOne` via `Shared/UiTheme.lua`. Use that when unsure.

## Organization
- One system = one owner script + named helpers.
- Update `docs/SYSTEMS_INDEX.md` in the same change as new/renamed systems.
- Prefer checklists in `docs/CHECKLISTS.md` for repeating work.
- Stable logs: `[PLOT]`, `[GRID]`, `[PERSIST]`, `[DECOR]`, `[INV]`.

## Edit surface
- Match existing patterns; do not refactor adjacent systems while fixing X.
- Update docs when behavior or ownership changes; stale docs are worse than short accurate ones.
